A||||22||Formula88||New RED gauges!||||10||
Z||000000||Formula88||04-01-2001||02:45 AM||||Well, with LZeitgeist's help, we took out the instrument cluster of my '88 Formula this weekend.  The orange backlighting for the gauges is from white lights reflecting off of an orange panel.  Well, it's supposed to be red, like the new Pontiacs, but has faded over time.  We took flourescent red vinyl, and covered all the orange areas.  To get a little better lighting, we also covered as much of the white plastic inside the cluster that we could get to.  Did the same thing with the gauge pod on the console.  Now, when I turn on my lights, the dash glows in a bright red!  It's much better looking than the faded orange I had before, and it matches the climate control backlighting again!  I highly recommend this to anyone with "orange" dash lights.  ||||reg||10
Z||000001||danny boy||04-01-2001||02:48 AM||||Cool, so it does work. I pondered doing mine in green to match the stereo.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||04-01-2001||03:01 AM||||Well, since the color comes from the backing, any color "should" work, but don't take my word for it.  Try it out and see, just make sure you can reverse it if you think it's butt-ugly.  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||04-01-2001||09:10 AM||||I have just done mine in green Dannyboy.<BR>I have also reproduced the gauge face panels in white with black lettering, all backlit green. Was quite a job to get it right but worth it. <BR>Am thinking about reproducing them in red, white or original black with a choice of backlit colours, anyone interested?<P>In the process of putting it all back together now. Whole dash has changed also, silver switching carbon fibre panels where the silver ones used to be, silver dash bolts and lots of other detail.<P>Will be posting pics of the completed dash and interior layout in the next 10 days for comments.<P>Cheers<BR>Jim  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
